    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d19">

                <pb facs="0095" n="71" xml:id="pg71"/>

                <head>19. National Security Council Report<anchor n="1" xml:id="d19-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">NSC 5515/1</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1955-04-01">April 1, 1955</date>.</hi></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">STUDY OF POSSIBLE HOSTILE SOVIET ACTIONS</p>
                <p>Note by the Executive Secretary to the National Security Council</p>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>REFERENCES</head>
                    <item>A. NSC Action No. 1260–c</item>
                    <item>B. NSC 5438</item>
                    <item>C. NSC 5515</item>
                    <item>D. NSC Action No. 1366<anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d19-f2"/></item>
                </list>
                <p>The National Security Council, the Secretary of the Treasury, the Acting
                    Director, Bureau of the Budget, and Mr. J. Walter Yeagley
                    for the Attorney General, at the 243rd Council meeting on March 31, 1955,<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d19-f3"/> noted the Study contained in NSC 5515, amended as set forth in NSC Action No. 1366–b, and enclosed herewith as NSC 5515/1.</p>
                <p>Because of the sensitivity of the information therein, this Study is being given
                    a limited distribution; <hi rendition="#italic">it is requested that special
                        security precautions be observed in its handling and that access to it be
                        limited on a strict need-to-know basis</hi>.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">James S. Lay,
                                Jr.</hi><anchor n="4" xml:id="d19-f4"/></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d19-a1.xml" xpointer="d19-a1"/>
